# Crockpot API — /units
#
# Same shape as requests/item-categories.http: GET is public, POST/PATCH/
# DELETE are ADMIN-only via middleware.RequireRole("ADMIN") — its 401/403
# behavior is already covered by internal/middleware's own unit tests, so
# this file focuses on the wiring: public read, ADMIN CRUD happy path,
# and the 409/404 translations, run against a live server + real DB.
#
# Reuses the same one-time ADMIN bump as item-categories.http (see
# requests/README.md) — no separate setup needed if you've already run
# that file.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Login (ADMIN account)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Login, to get a token for the checks below.
# @name login
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL",
  "password": "correcthorsebattery"
}

###

@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  GET /units (public)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — no token needed, returns the seeded units ordered by name
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/units

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  POST /units (ADMIN)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 201 — creates the unit this file exercises below
# @name create
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/units
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-unit",
  "abbreviation": "htu"
}

###

@unitId = {{create.response.body.id}}

### 🚫 409 name_taken — same name as above, different abbreviation
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/units
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-unit",
  "abbreviation": "htu-2"
}

###

### 🚫 409 abbreviation_taken — different name, same abbreviation as above
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/units
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-unit-2",
  "abbreviation": "htu"
}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  PATCH /units/:id (ADMIN)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — partial update, name only
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/units/{{unitId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-unit-renamed"
}

###

### 🚫 404 not_found — a random id that doesn't exist
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/units/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "doesn't matter"
}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  DELETE /units/:id (ADMIN)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 204 — deletes the unit created above (also this file's cleanup)
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/units/{{unitId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 🚫 404 not_found — already deleted by the request above
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/units/{{unitId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Cleanup
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Nothing dangling: the ✅ 204 delete above already removes the one
### unit this file creates, so a re-run from a clean server behaves the
### same way twice. No separate ADMIN-bump revert needed here — see
### item-categories.http's Cleanup section if you want to revert that.
